// A test that FAILS on purpose, so the whole failure REPORT of a shape-subject
// `testing.check` is compared byte for byte.
//
// # Why a deliberately red fixture exists at all
//
// `tests/` contains no program that fails an assertion. The differential
// sweep therefore compares only what a passing case prints, and reads `0 DIFFED`
// no matter how wrong a failure renders — three live divergences were found in
// this exact surface on the day this was written, all of them invisible to the
// sweep. The only way to compare failure output is to produce some.
//
// This file is NOT in the corpus and is never run by `nomi test tests`.
// It is reached only by TestPinned_CheckShapeFailureReport, whose whole subject
// is that the two paths agree about a NON-ZERO exit and the text above it.
//
// # What it compares that check_shape.nomi cannot
//
// check_shape.nomi reads the failure's FIELDS, which pins each value. This one
// pins the whole rendered object: the second case destructures a failing check
// with `assert Ok(_) = …`, so the report's `actual:` row is `value.Inspect` of
// the entire `AssertionFailure` VALUE — eight fields including two `Maybe`s and
// two `List`s, composed and SORTED, built independently by
// value.StructVal.Display and by rt.InspectStruct. That is the widest
// disagreement surface in the family and no field-by-field assertion reaches it.
import std/testing

fn find_name(id: Int): Maybe<String> {
    if id == 1 { Some("Ada") } else { None }
}

test "a shape check that holds keeps the whole file honest" {
    assert Ok(found) = testing.check(find_name(1))
    assert found
}

test "a failing shape check renders its own failure value" {
    assert Ok(_) = testing.check(find_name(2))
}
